#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:66
#, no-c-format
msgid "Introduction"
msgstr "Introduccion"

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&khexedit; is an editor for the raw data of binary files. It includes find/"
"replace functions, bookmarks, many configuration options, drag and drop "
"support and other powerful features."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:75
#, no-c-format
msgid "Starting &khexedit;"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Type <userinput><command>khexedit</command></userinput> at a command prompt "
"or select <guimenuitem>Binary Editor</guimenuitem> from the "
"<guisubmenu>Utilities</guisubmenu> group in the <guimenu>KDE start menu</"
"guimenu>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:81
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The standard &Qt; and &kde; command line options are available, and can be "
"listed by entering <userinput><command>khexedit</command> <option>--help</"
"option></userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid "Other command line options are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:87
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<option><replaceable>&lt;file&gt;</replaceable></option> - open the "
"specified file"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<option>--offset</option> <replaceable>&lt;offset&gt;</replaceable> jump to "
"position <replaceable>&lt;offset&gt;</replaceable> in the opened file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: index.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid "&khexedit; In A Nutshell"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The main &khexedit; window has the following components: menu bar, toolbar, "
"offset column, data editor window, text field, search bar, conversion field "
"and status bar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: screeninfo
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "<screeninfo>&khexedit; Screen</screeninfo>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "<phrase>&khexedit; Screen</phrase>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When a document is opened, the bytes are displayed in hexadecimal format in "
"the data editor window. The data can be edited, cut, copied, pasted, dragged "
"and dropped much as text is in an text editor or word processor. A cursor "
"marks the current position. Pressing the <keycap>Insert</keycap> key toggles "
"between overwrite and insert text entry modes. The data can also be "
"displayed as octal, binary or decimal values, by choosing the desired format "
"in the <guimenu>View</guimenu> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:123
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The offset column on the left indicates the position of a particular byte in "
"the file. The text field on the right displays the <acronym>ASCII</acronym> "
"encoding of the file. The cursor position and edits in the data editor "
"window are reflected in the text field. The text field can also be edited, "
"and those changes are reflected in the data editor window."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:129
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The search bar allows the user to search for a specific value -- "
"hexadecimal, octal, binary, decimal or text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:132
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The conversion field displays the value of the byte at the cursor position "
"in a variety of bases. It also displays the value of all standard data types "
"starting at the cursor."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: index.docbook:136
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Multiple documents can be open at the same time but only one can be active. "
"Use the <guimenu>Documents</guimenu> menu to select which document will be "
"active."
msgstr ""

